<p>(A) Pro forma amounts exclude the effect of the proceeds from life insurance totaling $5.0 million in the second quarter ended July 29, 1995.  In addition, pro forma amounts assume the public offering and the related transactions including the $6.1 million Debenture repurchase, the Series C exchange, which resulted in a non cash charge of $10 million and the interest rate reduction of 1/2 of 1% on the Revolving Credit Facility occurred immediately prior to the beginning of the 1995 fiscal year.</p>
<p>Excluding these pro forma adjustments, net income applicable to common shares was $3,534,000 for the year ended February 3, 1996 and the net income per share applicable to common shares for 1995 was $0.53.</p>
